 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! ============================================================                  
 INPUT CARD>! Why this file exists                                                          
 INPUT CARD>! ============================================================                  
 INPUT CARD>! A forum reply questioned the ~274 Hartree energy difference we found          
 INPUT CARD>! between our wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water) molecular energy (-491.67) and      
 INPUT CARD>! the energy reported in the original (lower-level) IRC source file             
 INPUT CARD>! (-765.88) at the same geometry. Re-checking this:                             
 INPUT CARD>! - The arithmetic is correct (-765.8776395 - (-491.6712565) = -274.2).         
 INPUT CARD>! - The CML file's molecule was confirmed identical: 13 atoms, Cl/C/C/O/H/H/    
 INPUT CARD>!   O/O/H/H/H/H/H, same composition, same electron count (60).                  
 INPUT CARD>! - A back-of-envelope sum of literature non-relativistic atomic HF energies    
 INPUT CARD>!   for this composition (Cl approx -459.5, C approx -37.7 x2, O approx         
 INPUT CARD>!   -74.8 x3, H approx -0.5 x7) gives approximately -763 Hartree for the        
 INPUT CARD>!   separated atoms -- very close to the CML's -765.88, and NOT close to        
 INPUT CARD>!   our own -491.67.                                                            
 INPUT CARD>! - This is NOT explained by an accidental ECP: GAMESS explicitly reports       
 INPUT CARD>!   NUMBER OF ELECTRONS = 60 in every one of our runs (an ECP replacing         
 INPUT CARD>!   Cl's Ne core would show a reduced count, e.g. 50), and our own $clbas       
 INPUT CARD>!   block has an appropriately tight core exponent (69507.99) for Cl's 1s       
 INPUT CARD>!   shell, consistent with genuine all-electron treatment.                      
 INPUT CARD>! - Also confirmed NOT a "forgot to add nuclear repulsion" bookkeeping          
 INPUT CARD>!   error: THE NUCLEAR REPULSION ENERGY IS 292.6267568387 is a SEPARATELY       
 INPUT CARD>!   printed quantity, and GAMESS's "FINAL ... ENERGY IS" line already           
 INPUT CARD>!   includes it by standard convention (self-consistent: a very negative        
 INPUT CARD>!   electronic energy plus positive nuclear repulsion gives the reported        
 INPUT CARD>!   total, as expected).                                                        
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! This points at something specific to how our own basis/setup describes        
 INPUT CARD>! chlorine, since Cl's atomic energy alone (~-459.5) is close in magnitude      
 INPUT CARD>! to a large fraction of the unexplained gap. Rather than keep reasoning        
 INPUT CARD>! from recalled reference numbers, this file tests it directly and              
 INPUT CARD>! empirically: an isolated Cl atom, gas phase, no PCM, no molecule, no          
 INPUT CARD>! optimizer -- using our EXACT $clbas block (copied verbatim from               
 INPUT CARD>! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPe.inp, not retyped, to rule out a new                
 INPUT CARD>! transcription error). If our basis/setup is fine, the reported energy         
 INPUT CARD>! should land close to the literature non-relativistic reference                
 INPUT CARD>! (approximately -459.5 Hartree for HF; DFT should be in a similar overall      
 INPUT CARD>! ballpark, not off by hundreds of Hartree). If it comes out dramatically       
 INPUT CARD>! different, that pinpoints the problem directly and unambiguously.             
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Cl ground state is 2P (one unpaired electron in the 3p shell), so this        
 INPUT CARD>! uses SCFTYP=UHF (doublet, MULT=2). Note: ROHF was tried first but requires    
 INPUT CARD>! explicit NSETO/NPAIR orbital-coupling input for chlorine's genuinely          
 INPUT CARD>! degenerate 3p5 open shell (5 electrons across 3 degenerate p-orbitals) --     
 INPUT CARD>! plain MULT=2 alone isn't enough information for ROHF's coupling scheme,       
 INPUT CARD>! and GAMESS aborted with "DIMENSIONS EXCEEDED". UHF sidesteps this (fills      
 INPUT CARD>! alpha/beta orbitals independently, no coupling setup needed) and is fine      
 INPUT CARD>! for this purpose -- a rough energy-magnitude sanity check, not a              
